TASK 5: INDIVIDUAL CASE SAFETY REPORT (ICSR)

1. Introduction

An Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR) is a structured report containing information about a suspected adverse drug reaction experienced by an individual patient after the administration of a medicinal product.

ICSRs are important in pharmacovigilance because they help identify, evaluate, document and monitor the safety of medicines.

2. Objectives

- To understand the structure and importance of an ICSR.
- To identify and document adverse drug reactions.
- To assess the seriousness and severity of an ADR.
- To evaluate the expectedness of the reaction.
- To perform causality assessment using WHO-UMC criteria.
- To understand the responsibilities of a Drug Safety Associate.

